    "body": "## Summary\n- persist an auditable `paymentReceivedAt` fact for successfully claimed publication payments\n- persist a coarse owner-safe `recoveryReason` when Stripe succeeds but the job cannot be safely created\n- distinguish late successful Stripe settlement after cancellation without resurrecting the job\n- expose the recovery contract in `JobPublicationResponse`\n- make the Stripe return page explain wallet-safe recovery outcomes and poll cancelled redirects for a late signed webhook\n- add Flyway V43, backend regression coverage, publication-payment smoke assertions and documentation\n\n## Financial invariants\n- no new balance mutation path: Stripe funding still goes through the existing payment ledger\n- wallet reservation restoration still uses the idempotent `JOB_PUBLICATION_RELEASE` operation\n- mismatched amount/currency/metadata is rejected before ledger mutation and before `paymentReceivedAt` is recorded\n- late payment never recreates a cancelled or expired publication\n- recovery metadata is owner-scoped and contains no serialized job payload, private location, route details or Stripe credentials\n\n## Commits\n1. `payments: persist publication settlement recovery outcome`\n2. `web: explain post-payment publication recovery`\n3. `ci: seed complete publication settlement outcome`\n\n## CI note\nThe first exact-head run exposed a stale payments-ledger smoke fixture that directly seeded `PAYMENT_RECEIVED` without the new settlement metadata. The production constraint was kept strict; the fixture was corrected on this branch to seed `payment_received_at` plus the historical-safe `UNSPECIFIED` recovery reason. The new exact head was then revalidated from scratch.\n\n## Exact-head validation (`40c1c1a8296c4399fa64e4e7402c399f2e7ff225`)\n- CI: success\n- Web verify: production dependency audit + lint + build success\n- API verify: Maven verify success\n- Containers and runtime smoke: success\n- Job publication payment smoke: success\n- Payments ledger smoke: success\n- Platform fee settlement smoke: success\n",
